<!--Post: 2551--><!--Time: 1103781536-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2551"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tornado<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tornado<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 22, 2004 - 9:58 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I was just dwelling on the mystery tonight when this thought came to me.  The properties where the crimes were committed...were they rentals?  Maybe this guy worked at the records office in the Courthouse and had access to rental property records, he then went and observed who lived in a property, then went back and did the crime.  Possibly he posed as a handy man working for the landlord...because if he worked at the courthouse, he would have had access to the owners name...he in turn could have went to the home and said your landlord; Mr So And So sent me to fix etc etc etc.  Anyway just a idea...what do you all think?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2551-->
<!--Post: 2578--><!--Time: 1103824537-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2578"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dee<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dee<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 23, 2004 - 9:55 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If any of the homes WERE rentals, that would explain the &#34;no forced entry&#34;.  He would have had a key.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2578-->
<!--Post: 2579--><!--Time: 1103824770-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2579"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Wichitagirl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Wichitagirl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 23, 2004 - 9:59 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->true tornaso im thinking he was a handyman also. i believe most of the houses were rentals<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2579-->
<!--Post: 2582--><!--Time: 1103827015-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2582"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dee<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dee<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 23, 2004 - 10:36 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Do you know if anyone has looked up the deeds on the addresses of the murder scenes?  That is all public record and would tell who owned the property.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2582-->
<!--Post: 2612--><!--Time: 1103842386-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2612"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tornado<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tornado<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 23, 2004 - 2:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I will call downtown to records on Monday and see if I can get the information on ownership and dates of the properties.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2612-->
<!--Post: 2769--><!--Time: 1104096969-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2769"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Canada<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Canada<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, December 26, 2004 - 1:36 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This is a great idea. A person who was in charge of rental properties would indeed have a key and would know the lay-out of the house &#40;bedrooms, telephone lines, etc&#41;. <BR>I was also thinking about real estate agents. They too would have keys. Who was the one handling the sale/rental of these homes?Sometimes if a house is up for sale and it does not sell immediately the homeowner rents it out while at the same time allowing it to be shown by real estate agents. Something to wonder about.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2769-->
<!--Post: 2911--><!--Time: 1104261850-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2911"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tornado<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tornado<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 28, 2004 - 11:24 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I called the records office and was unable to attain the information as to who owned the properties at the time of the killings.  I will try to find time to go to the library and go through the old R.L. Polk directories to find out if indeed they were all rental properties.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2911-->
<!--Post: 2978--><!--Time: 1104351745-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2978"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Secret_squirrel<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Secret_squirrel<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 12:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It sounds like your on to something Tornado.  What Im about to tell you may be a long shot and records may be different in your area and you may hit a dead end. <BR> <BR>Try your local fire department.  Some FD&#39;s keep records of property owners for the purposes of contacting them in the event of an emergency at their property.  I highly doubt that their records would go back that far but some bigger departments have an archive database.  However, run cards/report would most likely be kept as far back as possible provided the FD had good record keeping skills.  If the Fire/Police/EMS depts ever ran a call to the addresses in question the occupant and building owner would be on the report. Also try your local college or University.  Some schools have housing fairs for new students to find housing and have a list of respectable and reliable landlords.  Again, I doubt any records go back as far the 70&#39;s but it may be worth a look.  Good Luck!!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2978-->
</table></td></tr></table>
